{"name":"Mana","hex":"#b09737","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mana","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Power, prestige; specifically, a form of supernatural energy in Polynesian religion that inheres in things or people. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Magical energy."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of mina (“ancient unit of weight or currency”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mana"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mana (Oceanic cultures)","blocks":[{"text":"In Melanesian and Polynesian cultures, mana is a supernatural force that permeates the universe. Anyone or anything can have mana. They believed it to be a cultivation or possession of energy and power, rather than being a source of power. It is an intentional force."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mana_(Oceanic_cultures)","wikidata":"Q859517"},{"title":"Manna","blocks":[{"text":"Manna, sometimes or archaically spelled mana, is described in the Bible and the Quran as an edible substance that God bestowed upon the Israelites while they were wandering the desert during the 40-year period that followed the Exodus and preceded the conquest of Canaan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Tissot_The_Gathering_of_the_Manna_%28color%29.jpg/330px-Tissot_The_Gathering_of_the_Manna_%28color%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manna","wikidata":"Q241156"},{"title":"Mana (series)","blocks":[{"text":"The Mana series, known in Japan as Seiken Densetsu , is an action role-playing game series created by Koichi Ishii, with development formerly from Square, and is currently owned by Square Enix. The series began in 1991 as Final Fantasy Adventure, a Game Boy handheld side story to Square's flagship franchise Final Fantasy. The Final Fantasy elements were subsequently dropped starting with the second installment, Secret of Mana, in order to become its own series. It has grown to include games of various genres within the fictional world of Mana, with recurring stories involving a world tree, its associated holy sword, and the fight against forces that would steal their power. Several character designs, creatures, and musical themes reappear frequently."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mana_(series)","wikidata":"Q587964"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/StateLibQld_1_116272_Southern_Cross_%28ship%29.jpg/500px-StateLibQld_1_116272_Southern_Cross_%28ship%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/StateLibQld_1_116272_Southern_Cross_%28ship%29.jpg/500px-StateLibQld_1_116272_Southern_Cross_%28ship%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The 1891 Southern Cross, one of the ships at Norfolk Island's Melanesian Mission where Codrington taught and worked","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStateLibQld_1_116272_Southern_Cross_(ship).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Pine_branch_with_Marchalina_hellenica_honeydew.jpg/500px-Pine_branch_with_Marchalina_hellenica_honeydew.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Pine_branch_with_Marchalina_hellenica_honeydew.jpg/1280px-Pine_branch_with_Marchalina_hellenica_honeydew.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Pine_branch_with_Marchalina_hellenica_honeydew.jpg/500px-Pine_branch_with_Marchalina_hellenica_honeydew.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pine branch with Marchalina hellenica honeydew","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APine_branch_with_Marchalina_hellenica_honeyd